From: Christian Murphy <christian.murphy.42@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 02:52:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Prove the link round trip down to segments

Lean 4.35.0's standard library proves Nat.toNat?_repr, so String.toNat? inverts toString for a Nat capture. With it, dispatch_pathOf shows that dispatching a link's decoded segments calls the handler with the values passed to the link function. applyLink_linkFor shows that the link is those segments, encoded and joined by "/". Examples still cover splitting a link back into segments.

Signed-off-by: Christian Murphy <christian.murphy.42@gmail.com>
